---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Send any request to the Holst API, for an endpoint no command covers.
GET is sent at once. Any other method may change what cannot be undone, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst api <method> <path> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  method   The HTTP method: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH or DELETE
  path     The path from the root, for example /gapi/current_user

FLAGS
  -q, --query key=value   A query parameter, repeat for several
      --body body         The request body: a JSON string, @file to read a file, - for stdin
  -y, --yes               Confirm a change other than GET; without it only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run           Show the request; send nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst api GET /gapi/current_user
  $ holst api PATCH /gapi/channel/<id> --body @body.json -y

LEARN MORE
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
